PREAMBLE

  This license governs software that intervenes in the operation of a
computer. The software it was written for selects and terminates
processes to recover from memory commit exhaustion, and when recovery
is impossible it deliberately crashes the operating system with a
diagnostic bugcheck, so that the failure is recorded instead of
suffered silently.

  The license is permissive in the manner of the MIT and Expat
licenses: you may use, study, modify, and redistribute the software,
including for commercial purposes, on any machine you are entitled to
administer. It differs from those licenses in deliberate ways, each
grounded in what the software does:

  First, a tool that kills processes and bugchecks machines must never
be ambiguous about which code is running. Modified builds must carry
their modifications on their face and must not travel under the
original name.

  Second, the warnings are part of the work. No distributor may strip
them, soften them, or bury them where a user will not meet them before
the software meets their processes.

  Third, the software is never armed by default, and it is never
deployed where a deliberate crash could cost lives.

  The precise terms and conditions follow.


TERMS AND CONDITIONS

0. Definitions.

  "This License" refers to version 1 of The Last Resort License.

  "The Software" refers to the copyrightable work licensed under this
License, in source and binary form, together with its documentation,
installer scripts, and test tooling.

  "You" is the licensee. "Modify", "Distribute", and "Contribution"
carry their usual copyright meanings; a Contribution is any work
intentionally submitted by a copyright holder for inclusion in the
Software.

  "Safety Notices" means every statement shipped with the Software --
in source comments, documentation, installers, or scripts -- warning
that the Software may terminate processes without the consent of the
processes' owners, may deliberately crash the operating system when
recovery fails, and must only be exercised on machines the operator is
prepared to lose.

  "Enforcement" means the operating mode in which the Software is
permitted to terminate processes or raise bugchecks: the armed state
in the reference implementation.

