make, have made, use, and distribute that contributor's Contributions,
to the extent those Contributions are covered by patent claims the
contributor has the right to license.

2. Conditions of Redistribution.

  You may Distribute copies, modified or unmodified, provided that:

  a. every copy carries this License, the copyright notice above, and
     the Safety Notices, verbatim and conspicuously;

  b. every Modified Work carries a prominent notice stating that You
     changed it, the date of the change, and a one-line summary of
     what the change does to victim selection, thresholds, watchdog
     behavior, or bugcheck conditions;

  c. no Modified Work that alters victim selection, kill thresholds,
     watchdog timing, safety checks, or bugcheck behavior is
     Distributed under the original name of the Software; You must
     give such a work a name of Your own that does not contain the
     original name;

  d. no Safety Notice is removed, weakened, reworded to reduce its
     clarity, or relocated behind an interaction the user can skip;
     and

  e. the Software is not configured to begin Enforcement on
     installation or boot without explicit, documented, local
     administrative action taken by the machine's operator after
     installation. The reference implementation installs disarmed;
     distributions must not invert that default.

3. Crash-Testing Builds.

  Facilities whose purpose is to trigger bugchecks on demand -- in the
reference implementation, the manual-crash ioctl and its command-line
front end -- may be built, used, and Distributed only in builds that
are clearly and permanently distinguishable from normal builds, by
configuration name, binary naming, or equivalent, and only with their
test-only status stated wherever the build is offered. They must not
be present in any build presented as a production or release build.

4. Deployment Covenant.

  In consideration of the rights granted here, You agree not to deploy
the Software, modified or unmodified, on any system where a deliberate
crash, a reboot, or the termination of a process could reasonably be
expected to cause death, serious bodily injury, or catastrophic
physical damage, including without limitation life-support, medical,
aviation, rail-signalling, nuclear, weapons, and industrial-control
systems. The Software's own documentation says the same thing in
plainer words: do not pressure-test a machine containing anything You
care about. This covenant binds every recipient downstream of You and
survives redistribution.

5. Indemnity for Distributors and Operators.

  If You Distribute the Software, or operate it in Enforcement on
behalf of others, You agree to defend and indemnify the authors and
copyright holders of the Software against claims arising from Your
modifications, Your distribution, or Your operation of the Software,
except to the extent a claim rests on the unmodified Software as
Distributed by the original authors.

6. Termination.

  Your rights under this License terminate automatically if You
violate its conditions. If the violation is cured within thirty (30)
days of Your learning of it, and no Safety Notice was suppressed in
the meantime, Your rights are reinstated without further action.
Recipients who received copies from You retain their rights while they
remain compliant.

